{{- /*
  /_redirects -- the host-level redirect map (Cloudflare Pages, GitLab Pages,
  Netlify), published at the site root.

  This template does every byte of the printing, and redirects/lines.html does
  every decision. The split is forced rather than stylistic: a partial named
  .html is parsed as an HTML template, so text it EMITS arrives here escaped
  (`&#34;` for a quote, `&amp;` for an ampersand in a query string), while a
  value it RETURNS crosses untouched.

  The file is published whether or not the module is switched on, because an
  unwired output format and an empty file mean different things to a deployment
  and only one of them is a state that can be built against.
*/ -}}
{{- $lines := partial "url-retirement/redirects/lines.html" (dict "page" .) -}}
{{- with $lines -}}{{ delimit . "\n" }}
{{ end -}}
